concept:act-sch-1-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Subsection 31(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) A person may apply for an order under section 29 or 29A if a *restraining order that covers property in which the person claims an *interest has been made.  (1A) An application under subsection (1):  (a) must be made to the court that made the *restraining order; and  (b) may be made at any time after the restraining order is made. Note: The heading to section 31 is altered by omitting “notice of the order” and substituting “restraining order has been made”. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Proceeds of crime  Schedule 1 Exclusion, recovery and compensation  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2) 2010          7" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) A person may apply for an order under section 29 or 29A if a *restraining order that covers property in which the person claims an *interest has been made.  (1A) An application under subsection (1):  (a) must be made to the court that made the *restraining order; and  (b) may be made at any time after the restraining order is made. Note: The heading to section 31 is altered by omitting “notice of the order” and substituting “restraining order has been made”. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Proceeds of crime  Schedule 1 Exclusion, recovery and compensation  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2) 2010          7"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-16-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-16-ss-1a ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.12" .
doc:sch-1-sec-16 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "16 Subsection 31(1)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (1) A person may apply for an order under section 29 or 29A if a *restraining order that covers property in which the person claims an *interest has been made.  (1A) An application under subsection (1):  (a) must be made to the court that made the *restraining order; and  (b) may be made at any time after the restraining order is made. Note: The heading to section 31 is altered by omitting “notice of the order” and substituting “restraining order has been made”. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Proceeds of crime  Schedule 1 Exclusion, recovery and compensation  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2) 2010          7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

