    values:originalText "(3) The court may give the person leave to apply if the court is satisfied that:  (a) if subparagraph (2)(b)(i) applies—the person had a good reason for not making an application under section 29 or 94; or  (b) if subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) applies—the person now has evidence relevant to the person’s application under this section that was not available at the time of the hearing; or  (c) in either case—there are other special grounds for granting the leave." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The court may give the person leave to apply if the court is satisfied that:  (a) if subparagraph (2)(b)(i) applies—the person had a good reason for not making an application under section 29 or 94; or  (b) if subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) applies—the person now has evidence relevant to the person’s application under this section that was not available at the time of the hearing; or  (c) in either case—there are other special grounds for granting the leave."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a7a6375993e2088597778e3af8338c64774d09badf8ebeb3f9d2deba57a8f54c" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-1-sec-104 ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may give leave to apply under section 102 or 103" ;
