concept:act-sch-1-sec-18-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-18-2 ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010  (5) The *DPP may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing of the application.  (6) The *DPP must give the applicant notice of any grounds on which it proposes to contest the application. However, the DPP need not do so until it has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct *examinations in relation to the application.  (7) The application must not be heard until the *DPP has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct *examinations in relation to the application." ;
    skos:definition "(No. 2) 2010  (5) The *DPP may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing of the application.  (6) The *DPP must give the applicant notice of any grounds on which it proposes to contest the application. However, the DPP need not do so until it has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct *examinations in relation to the application.  (7) The application must not be heard until the *DPP has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct *examinations in relation to the application."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "23d7e039a71dea0a270c3327c8db336e95bb31d36f99c49215786eb4e903c065" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-18-2-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.24" .
doc:sch-1-sec-18-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "18 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010  (5) The *DPP may appear and adduce evidence at the hearing of the application.  (6) The *DPP must give the applicant notice of any grounds on which it proposes to contest the application. However, the DPP need not do so until it has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct *examinations in relation to the application.  (7) The application must not be heard until the *DPP has had a reasonable opportunity to conduct *examinations in relation to the application." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

