concept:act-sch-1-sec-180b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "180B Examination orders relating to applications for compensation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-180b ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an application for an order under section 77 or 94A (which deal with compensation) is made in relation to an *interest in property that has been or may be forfeited, the court to which the application is made may make an order (an examination order) for the *examination of any person including:  (a) a person who has or claims an *interest in the property; or  (b) the spouse or *de facto partner of a person referred to in paragraph (a); about the *affairs of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).  (2) The *examination order ceases to have effect when:  (a) the application is withdrawn; or  (b) the court makes a decision on the application." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an application for an order under section 77 or 94A (which deal with compensation) is made in relation to an *interest in property that has been or may be forfeited, the court to which the application is made may make an order (an examination order) for the *examination of any person including:  (a) a person who has or claims an *interest in the property; or  (b) the spouse or *de facto partner of a person referred to in paragraph (a); about the *affairs of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b).  (2) The *examination order ceases to have effect when:  (a) the application is withdrawn; or  (b) the court makes a decision on the application."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6145c9f6f642e1aeba83371a047b2b4c1ecb468989b1210e07646e92f8c50c8d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
