concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-40-2 ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010  (b) the application for the ancillary order was heard without notice having been given under subsection 39(3) following a request under subsection 39(3A).  (2) The application must be made within 14 days after the person was notified of the ancillary order.  (3) The applicant must give written notice of the application, and the grounds on which the revocation is sought, to any person who was entitled to make the application for the ancillary order (see subsection 39(2)).  (4) The effect of the ancillary order is stayed until the court determines the application.  (5) The court may revoke the ancillary order on application under subsection (1) if it considers it appropriate to do so.  (6) The court may have regard to any matter it considers appropriate in determining the application.  (7) If:  (a) the ancillary order directed a person to do a thing within a particular period; and  (b) an application is made to revoke the order under this section; the court may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, vary the order to extend that period by a specified period." ;
    skos:definition "(No. 2) 2010  (b) the application for the ancillary order was heard without notice having been given under subsection 39(3) following a request under subsection 39(3A).  (2) The application must be made within 14 days after the person was notified of the ancillary order.  (3) The applicant must give written notice of the application, and the grounds on which the revocation is sought, to any person who was entitled to make the application for the ancillary order (see subsection 39(2)).  (4) The effect of the ancillary order is stayed until the court determines the application.  (5) The court may revoke the ancillary order on application under subsection (1) if it considers it appropriate to do so.  (6) The court may have regard to any matter it considers appropriate in determining the application.  (7) If:  (a) the ancillary order directed a person to do a thing within a particular period; and  (b) an application is made to revoke the order under this section; the court may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, vary the order to extend that period by a specified period."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a76986b2c94a23e2125054501178e3dbe4ccc7281e9aba40ac30052ab3b61102" ;
    cof:pageNumber "46"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.46" .
doc:sch-1-sec-40-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "40 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010  (b) the application for the ancillary order was heard without notice having been given under subsection 39(3) following a request under subsection 39(3A).  (2) The application must be made within 14 days after the person was notified of the ancillary order.  (3) The applicant must give written notice of the application, and the grounds on which the revocation is sought, to any person who was entitled to make the application for the ancillary order (see subsection 39(2)).  (4) The effect of the ancillary order is stayed until the court determines the application.  (5) The court may revoke the ancillary order on application under subsection (1) if it considers it appropriate to do so.  (6) The court may have regard to any matter it considers appropriate in determining the application.  (7) If:  (a) the ancillary order directed a person to do a thing within a particular period; and  (b) an application is made to revoke the order under this section; the court may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, vary the order to extend that period by a specified period." ;
    cof:pageNumber "46"^^xsd:integer .

