concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "40(7) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-40-2-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) If:  (a) the ancillary order directed a person to do a thing within a particular period; and  (b) an application is made to revoke the order under this section; the court may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, vary the order to extend that period by a specified period." ;
    skos:definition "(7) If:  (a) the ancillary order directed a person to do a thing within a particular period; and  (b) an application is made to revoke the order under this section; the court may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, vary the order to extend that period by a specified period."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5cc660553e172b51f2ded4a611d02502289a4a302b328d11c889a504d3532681" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-1-sec-40-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "46"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may vary ancillary order to extend period if appropriate." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
