concept:act-sch-1-sec-318b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "318B Objection to admission of statements made at examination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-318b ;
    values:originalText "Adducing party to give notice  (1) A party (the adducing party) to a proceeding referred to in subsection 318A(1) may, not less than 14 days before the first day of the hearing of the proceeding, give another party to the proceeding written notice that the adducing party:  (a) will apply to have admitted in evidence in the proceeding specified statements made at an *examination; and  (b) for that purpose, will apply to have evidence of those statements admitted in the proceeding.  (2) The notice must set out, or be accompanied by a written record of, the specified statements. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 1  Proceeds of crime" ;
    skos:definition "Adducing party to give notice  (1) A party (the adducing party) to a proceeding referred to in subsection 318A(1) may, not less than 14 days before the first day of the hearing of the proceeding, give another party to the proceeding written notice that the adducing party:  (a) will apply to have admitted in evidence in the proceeding specified statements made at an *examination; and  (b) for that purpose, will apply to have evidence of those statements admitted in the proceeding.  (2) The notice must set out, or be accompanied by a written record of, the specified statements. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 1  Proceeds of crime"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b84a5d8177785b0854b9105f4672ccbf951129bb7311fd731cc67b7eea1543f1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-318b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-1-sec-318b-ss-2 ;
