concept:act-sch-2-sec-2010-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2010(5) 59"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-2010-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A constable or Commonwealth officer may make a thing seized under this Part, or the original or a copy of a document produced under Division 4B, available to:  (a) a State or Territory law enforcement agency; or  (b) an agency that has responsibility for:  (i) law enforcement in a foreign country; or  (ii) intelligence gathering for a foreign country; or  (iii) the security of a foreign country; to be used by that agency for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1), (2) or (3) and the purpose of any or all of the following (but not for any other purpose): ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 2  Search warrants" ;
    skos:definition "(5) A constable or Commonwealth officer may make a thing seized under this Part, or the original or a copy of a document produced under Division 4B, available to:  (a) a State or Territory law enforcement agency; or  (b) an agency that has responsibility for:  (i) law enforcement in a foreign country; or  (ii) intelligence gathering for a foreign country; or  (iii) the security of a foreign country; to be used by that agency for a purpose mentioned in subsection (1), (2) or (3) and the purpose of any or all of the following (but not for any other purpose): ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 2  Search warrants"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "28ff5c949ffde6f8c772b54f6d58091493ba29b97d4d9e901db4c60d0a84e423" ;
