doc:sch-2-sec-2010-3-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "2010(2) 63" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the Commissioner does not have to take those steps if:  (a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford evidence were instituted before the end of the 60 days and have not been completed (including an appeal to a court in relation to those proceedings); or  (b) the thing may be retained because of an order under section 3ZQZ; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 2  Search warrants" ;
