concept:act-sch-2-sec-64-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "64(2) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-64-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the Commissioner does not have to take those steps if:  (a) the Commissioner suspects on reasonable grounds that if the thing is returned to the owner, the thing is likely to be used by the owner or another person in the commission of a terrorist act, a terrorism offence or a serious offence; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Search warrants  Schedule 2 Seized things  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)" ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, the Commissioner does not have to take those steps if:  (a) the Commissioner suspects on reasonable grounds that if the thing is returned to the owner, the thing is likely to be used by the owner or another person in the commission of a terrorist act, a terrorism offence or a serious offence; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Search warrants  Schedule 2 Seized things  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bafe60d70fc1711ecdf07bb3e3a6c36c9afaf02d34bb1835d6b1b79315237a78" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-2-sec-64 ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commissioner does not have to take steps if suspecting terrorist act or serious offence Magistrate may order retention of thing for specified period." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
