concept:act-sch-2-sec-3la a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3LA Person with knowledge of a computer or a computer system to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-3la ;
    values:originalText "assist access etc.  (1) A constable may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any information or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow a constable to do one or more of the following:  (a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer or data storage device that:  (i) is on warrant premises; or  (ii) has been removed from warrant premises under subsection 3K(2) and is at another place for examination or processing; or  (iii) has been seized under this Division and is no longer on the warrant premises;  (b) copy data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data storage device, described in paragraph (a) to another data storage device;  (c) convert into documentary form or another form intelligible to a constable:  (i) data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data storage device, described in paragraph (a); or  (ii) data held in a data storage device to which the data was copied as described in paragraph (b); or  (iii) data held in a data storage device removed from warrant premises under subsection 3L(1A). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 2  Search warrants" ;
    skos:definition "assist access etc.  (1) A constable may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide any information or assistance that is reasonable and necessary to allow a constable to do one or more of the following:  (a) access data held in, or accessible from, a computer or data storage device that:  (i) is on warrant premises; or  (ii) has been removed from warrant premises under subsection 3K(2) and is at another place for examination or processing; or  (iii) has been seized under this Division and is no longer on the warrant premises;  (b) copy data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data storage device, described in paragraph (a) to another data storage device;  (c) convert into documentary form or another form intelligible to a constable:  (i) data held in, or accessible from, a computer, or data storage device, described in paragraph (a); or  (ii) data held in a data storage device to which the data was copied as described in paragraph (b); or  (iii) data held in a data storage device removed from warrant premises under subsection 3L(1A). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 2  Search warrants"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8a602f82677c85037e008d3ca76af9341d4eee29da4493cb86b5a51ff25143ae" ;
    cof:pageNumber "75"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A constable may apply to a magistrate for an order requiring a specified person to provide information or assistance." ;
    dc:description "reasonable and necessary information or assistance" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.75" ;
    cml:asserts concept:act-sch-2-sec-3la-norm .
