doc:sch-3-sec-84-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "84(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person discloses information about an individual; and  (b) the individual is undergoing assessment for inclusion in the NWPP at the time the information is disclosed; and  (c) if the individual were included in the NWPP following that assessment, the individual would be a Commonwealth participant or a Territory participant; and  (d) there is a risk that disclosure of the information will reveal that the individual is undergoing such assessment; and  (e) there is a risk that disclosure of the information will compromise the security of the individual. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-3-sec-84-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "84(5) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-84-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Subsections (1), (2), (3) and (4) do not apply to a disclosure by a person if:  (a) the person has been authorised by the Commissioner to make the disclosure; or  (b) the disclosure is made for the purpose of making a complaint, or providing information, to the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or  (c) the disclosure is made for the purpose of referring to the Integrity Commissioner, under the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006, an allegation or information that raises a corruption issue; or  (d) the disclosure is made for the purpose of:  (i) giving information that raises an AFP conduct or practices issue (within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979); or  (ii) investigating or resolving an AFP conduct or practices issue under Part V of that Act. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Subsections (1), (2), (3) and (4) do not apply to a disclosure by a person if:  (a) the person has been authorised by the Commissioner to make the disclosure; or  (b) the disclosure is made for the purpose of making a complaint, or providing information, to the Ombudsman under the Ombudsman Act 1976; or  (c) the disclosure is made for the purpose of referring to the Integrity Commissioner, under the Law Enforcement Integrity Commissioner Act 2006, an allegation or information that raises a corruption issue; or  (d) the disclosure is made for the purpose of:  (i) giving information that raises an AFP conduct or practices issue (within the meaning of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979); or  (ii) investigating or resolving an AFP conduct or practices issue under Part V of that Act. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8934a67d067ee7827e8ddcba52878c23217c78c3235ca4229ccf84d16ff25a9e" ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-3-sec-84 ;
