concept:act-sch-3-sec-69 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69 Saving provision—declarations of complementary witness"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-69 ;
    values:originalText "protection laws (1) A declaration made under paragraph (b) of the definition of complementary witness protection law in section 3 of the Witness Protection Act 1994 before the commencement of this item is not, and is taken never to have been, a legislative instrument. (2) If the declaration was in force just before the commencement of this item, the declaration has effect from that commencement, subject to subitem (1), as if it had been made under section 3AA of that Act as inserted by this Schedule. 70  Application—action in respect of former participants etc. The Commissioner may take action under subsection 13(5) of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as inserted by this Schedule, on or after the commencement of this item, whether the former participant concerned became a former participant before, on or after that commencement." ;
    skos:definition "protection laws (1) A declaration made under paragraph (b) of the definition of complementary witness protection law in section 3 of the Witness Protection Act 1994 before the commencement of this item is not, and is taken never to have been, a legislative instrument. (2) If the declaration was in force just before the commencement of this item, the declaration has effect from that commencement, subject to subitem (1), as if it had been made under section 3AA of that Act as inserted by this Schedule. 70  Application—action in respect of former participants etc. The Commissioner may take action under subsection 13(5) of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as inserted by this Schedule, on or after the commencement of this item, whether the former participant concerned became a former participant before, on or after that commencement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8949fb2f87cff1aa7c845ae6cad56b228107800c905dc587ffa40576ebf84e56" ;
    cof:pageNumber "101"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Saving provision—declarations of complementary witness" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.101" ;
    cml:asserts concept:act-sch-3-sec-69-norm .
concept:act-sch-3-sec-69-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:act-sch-3-sec-69 ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-3-sec-69 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "69 Saving provision—declarations of complementary witness" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "protection laws (1) A declaration made under paragraph (b) of the definition of complementary witness protection law in section 3 of the Witness Protection Act 1994 before the commencement of this item is not, and is taken never to have been, a legislative instrument. (2) If the declaration was in force just before the commencement of this item, the declaration has effect from that commencement, subject to subitem (1), as if it had been made under section 3AA of that Act as inserted by this Schedule. 70  Application—action in respect of former participants etc. The Commissioner may take action under subsection 13(5) of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as inserted by this Schedule, on or after the commencement of this item, whether the former participant concerned became a former participant before, on or after that commencement." ;
    cof:pageNumber "101"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-3-sec-71 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "71 Application—non-disclosure of former identity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-71 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Section 16 of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as amended by this Act, applies on and after the commencement of this item in relation to a pre-commencement permission given to a participant for a particular purpose as if it were a post-commencement permission given for the participant not to disclose his or her original identity for that purpose. (2) In this item: post-commencement permission means a permission given under paragraph 16(1)(b) of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as in force at the commencement of this item. pre-commencement permission means a permission given under paragraph 16(1)(b) of the Witness Protection Act 1994 before the commencement of this item. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 4  Criminal organisation and association offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Section 16 of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as amended by this Act, applies on and after the commencement of this item in relation to a pre-commencement permission given to a participant for a particular purpose as if it were a post-commencement permission given for the participant not to disclose his or her original identity for that purpose. (2) In this item: post-commencement permission means a permission given under paragraph 16(1)(b) of the Witness Protection Act 1994, as in force at the commencement of this item. pre-commencement permission means a permission given under paragraph 16(1)(b) of the Witness Protection Act 1994 before the commencement of this item. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 4  Criminal organisation and association offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f2609165fe747353c6b6c08fb3b07a5bc5f6db17d938889b9b4a705cab7a4fd6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "101"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Applicability of Witness Protection Act 1994 to pre-commencement permissions" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.101" ;
    cml:asserts concept:act-sch-3-sec-71-norm .
