concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-3 cml:asserts concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-3-logic-deontic-4 .
concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-3-logic-deontic-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Obligation" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Associating with someone who engages in an offence is an obligation for the first person" ;
    cml:premiseText "(a) the first person associates on 2 or more occasions with another person (the second person);..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The first person has an obligation to associate with the second person" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-3 cml:asserts concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-3-logic-argumentation-5 .
concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-3-logic-argumentation-5 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Argumentation ;
    cml:operator "Implication" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Associating with someone who engages in an offence implies that the first person is committing an offence" ;
    cml:premiseText "(b) the second person engages, or proposes to engage, in conduct (the second person’s conduct)..." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The associations imply that the first person is committing an offence" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::argumentation" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-4-sec-390-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "390 3  Associating in support of serious organised criminal activity" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person associates on 2 or more occasions with another person (the second person); and  (b) the second person engages, or proposes to engage, in conduct (the second person’s conduct) that constitutes, or is part of conduct constituting, an offence against any law; and  (c) the associations facilitate the engagement or proposed engagement by the second person in the second person’s conduct; and  (d) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (b) involves 2 or more persons; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (b) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years. Penalty: Imprisonment for 3 years. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 4  Criminal organisation and association offences" ;
    cof:pageNumber "107"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-4-sec-102 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "102 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-102 ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010 Repeat offence  (2) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person has previously been convicted of an offence against subsection (1); and  (b) the first person associates with another person (the second person); and  (c) the second person engages, or proposes to engage, in conduct (the second person’s conduct) that constitutes, or is part of conduct constituting, an offence against any law; and  (d) the association facilitates the engagement or proposed engagement by the second person in the second person’s conduct; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (c) involves 2 or more persons; and  (f) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (c) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years. Penalty: Imprisonment for 3 years. Knowledge fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (2)(c)  (3) The fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (2)(c) is knowledge (by the first person). Intention fault element for paragraphs (1)(c) and (2)(d)  (3A) The fault element for paragraphs (1)(c) and (2)(d) is intention (by the first person). Absolute liability  (4) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(e) and (2)(f). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Prosecution need not prove identity of certain persons  (5) In a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1) or (2), it is not necessary to prove the identity of any of the persons mentioned in paragraph (1)(d) or (2)(e). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Criminal organisation and association offences  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)" ;
    skos:definition "(No. 2) 2010 Repeat offence  (2) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person has previously been convicted of an offence against subsection (1); and  (b) the first person associates with another person (the second person); and  (c) the second person engages, or proposes to engage, in conduct (the second person’s conduct) that constitutes, or is part of conduct constituting, an offence against any law; and  (d) the association facilitates the engagement or proposed engagement by the second person in the second person’s conduct; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (c) involves 2 or more persons; and  (f) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (c) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years. Penalty: Imprisonment for 3 years. Knowledge fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (2)(c)  (3) The fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (2)(c) is knowledge (by the first person). Intention fault element for paragraphs (1)(c) and (2)(d)  (3A) The fault element for paragraphs (1)(c) and (2)(d) is intention (by the first person). Absolute liability  (4) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(e) and (2)(f). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Prosecution need not prove identity of certain persons  (5) In a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1) or (2), it is not necessary to prove the identity of any of the persons mentioned in paragraph (1)(d) or (2)(e). ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Criminal organisation and association offences  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "653f260229ee0088f5deea3b355ec78a3e521aaa8747726cd5451f931dfeb7d2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-4-sec-102-ss-2 ;
