concept:act-sch-4-sec-390-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "390 6  Directing activities of a criminal organisation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-390-7 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person directs one or more activities of an organisation; and  (b) either:  (i) the activity or activities directed aid; or  (ii) there is a risk that the activity or activities directed will aid;  the organisation to engage in conduct constituting an offence against any law; and  (c) the organisation consists of 2 or more persons; and  (d) the organisation’s aims or activities include facilitating the engagement in conduct, or engaging in conduct, constituting ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Criminal organisation and association offences  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person directs one or more activities of an organisation; and  (b) either:  (i) the activity or activities directed aid; or  (ii) there is a risk that the activity or activities directed will aid;  the organisation to engage in conduct constituting an offence against any law; and  (c) the organisation consists of 2 or more persons; and  (d) the organisation’s aims or activities include facilitating the engagement in conduct, or engaging in conduct, constituting ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Criminal organisation and association offences  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "37d6234fbef05576b400b644eb0c13a11fba16a8ad3839ccb7a8a76de39132ae" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Directing activities of an organisation constituting an offence against any law." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "act.pdf, p.112" ;
