    cof:title "390 6  Directing activities of a criminal organisation" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person directs one or more activities of an organisation; and  (b) either:  (i) the activity or activities directed aid; or  (ii) there is a risk that the activity or activities directed will aid;  the organisation to engage in conduct constituting an offence against any law; and  (c) the organisation consists of 2 or more persons; and  (d) the organisation’s aims or activities include facilitating the engagement in conduct, or engaging in conduct, constituting ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Criminal organisation and association offences  Schedule 4  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act (No. 2)" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-4-sec-2010-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2010 107"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-2010-6 ;
    values:originalText "an offence against any law that is, or would if committed be, for the benefit of the organisation; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (d) is an offence against any law punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years; and  (f) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (b) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 12 months. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person directs one or more activities of an organisation; and  (b) the activity or activities directed constitute an offence against any law; and  (c) the organisation consists of 2 or more persons; and  (d) the organisation’s aims or activities include facilitating the engagement in conduct, or engaging in conduct, constituting an offence against any law that is, or would if committed be, for the benefit of the organisation; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (d) is an offence against any law punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years; and  (f) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (b) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 12 months. Penalty: Imprisonment for 15 years.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(e) and (f) and (2)(e) and (f). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2.  (4) To avoid doubt, the person may be convicted of an offence against subsection (1) because of a risk that the activity or activities directed will aid the organisation as described in paragraph (1)(b) even if the activity or activities do not actually aid the organisation in that way. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 4  Criminal organisation and association offences" ;
    skos:definition "an offence against any law that is, or would if committed be, for the benefit of the organisation; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (d) is an offence against any law punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years; and  (f) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (b) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 12 months. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (2) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person directs one or more activities of an organisation; and  (b) the activity or activities directed constitute an offence against any law; and  (c) the organisation consists of 2 or more persons; and  (d) the organisation’s aims or activities include facilitating the engagement in conduct, or engaging in conduct, constituting an offence against any law that is, or would if committed be, for the benefit of the organisation; and  (e) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (d) is an offence against any law punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 years; and  (f) the offence against any law mentioned in paragraph (b) is a constitutionally covered offence punishable by imprisonment for at least 12 months. Penalty: Imprisonment for 15 years.  (3) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(e) and (f) and (2)(e) and (f). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2.  (4) To avoid doubt, the person may be convicted of an offence against subsection (1) because of a risk that the activity or activities directed will aid the organisation as described in paragraph (1)(b) even if the activity or activities do not actually aid the organisation in that way. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 4  Criminal organisation and association offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "00a9718c404a5231b3b62ce6b4b70744c90676d43ff6e652a7a311b6f3d9b020" ;
