concept:act-sch-5-sec-116 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "116 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-116 ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010 Extended application of sections 16.1, 16.2 and 16.3  (6) Section 16.1, except paragraph 16.1(1)(a), applies in relation to an offence against this Division (in addition to the application of that section apart from this subsection). Note: Section 16.1 requires the Attorney-General’s consent for prosecution of an offence if the alleged conduct occurred wholly in a foreign country in certain circumstances.  (7) Sections 16.2 and 16.3 apply for the purposes of this Division in the same way as they apply for the purposes of Part 2.7. Note: Section 16.2 treats the sending of things and electronic communications into and out of Australia as conduct occurring partly in Australia. Section 16.3 affects the meaning of Australia." ;
    skos:definition "(No. 2) 2010 Extended application of sections 16.1, 16.2 and 16.3  (6) Section 16.1, except paragraph 16.1(1)(a), applies in relation to an offence against this Division (in addition to the application of that section apart from this subsection). Note: Section 16.1 requires the Attorney-General’s consent for prosecution of an offence if the alleged conduct occurred wholly in a foreign country in certain circumstances.  (7) Sections 16.2 and 16.3 apply for the purposes of this Division in the same way as they apply for the purposes of Part 2.7. Note: Section 16.2 treats the sending of things and electronic communications into and out of Australia as conduct occurring partly in Australia. Section 16.3 affects the meaning of Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4f3b14a8b6d53c6a0500921a94214c080284ae991c88bc202e634a48a1cf2c39" ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-5-sec-116-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-5-sec-116-ss-7 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
