doc:sch-6-sec-20bi-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20BI(3) Appeals against some Victorian jury findings of unfitness to be" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Court of Appeal must allow the appeal if the court thinks that:  (a) the finding should be set aside because it is unreasonable or cannot be supported having regard to the evidence; or  (b) the order of the Supreme Court or County Court giving effect to the finding should be set aside because of a wrong decision on a question of law; or  (c) there was a miscarriage of justice. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011C00166  Schedule 6  Unfitness to plead" ;
    cof:pageNumber "127"^^xsd:integer .

concept:act-sch-6-sec-122 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "122 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious and Organised Crime) Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-122 ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2010  (4) Otherwise, the Court of Appeal must dismiss the appeal.  (5) Despite subsection (3), the Court of Appeal may dismiss the appeal if the Court of Appeal thinks that no substantial miscarriage of justice has occurred. Consequences if appeal allowed  (6) If the Court of Appeal allows the appeal:  (a) the accused may be tried for the federal offence; and  (b) the Court of Appeal may make orders for the custody or bail of the accused. Rules of court  (7) Rules of court for the Court of Appeal of Victoria may make provision relating to appeals under subsection (2) and proceedings relating to orders under paragraph (6)(b). Relationship with the rest of this Division  (8) This Division has effect subject to this section." ;
    skos:definition "(No. 2) 2010  (4) Otherwise, the Court of Appeal must dismiss the appeal.  (5) Despite subsection (3), the Court of Appeal may dismiss the appeal if the Court of Appeal thinks that no substantial miscarriage of justice has occurred. Consequences if appeal allowed  (6) If the Court of Appeal allows the appeal:  (a) the accused may be tried for the federal offence; and  (b) the Court of Appeal may make orders for the custody or bail of the accused. Rules of court  (7) Rules of court for the Court of Appeal of Victoria may make provision relating to appeals under subsection (2) and proceedings relating to orders under paragraph (6)(b). Relationship with the rest of this Division  (8) This Division has effect subject to this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "23d7e039a71dea0a270c3327c8db336e95bb31d36f99c49215786eb4e903c065" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-6-sec-122-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-6-sec-122-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-6-sec-122-ss-6 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:act-sch-6-sec-122-ss-7 ;
