concept:act-sch-10-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 After subsection 61B(8)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-10-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (8A) For the purposes of this section, if a person is convicted of an offence against this Act because of section 11.2A of the Criminal Code:  (a) the person is taken to have been convicted of an ancillary offence; and  (b) the offence that was committed because of that section is taken to be the primary offence to which the ancillary offence relates. Historic Shipwrecks Act 1976" ;
